<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒu.mu.ɑ">Jumu'ah</phoneme> briefing.</s> <s>The seventeenth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>The United States military has concluded it likely struck a girls' school in the Iranian town of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="miˈnɑb">Minab</phoneme>, killing a hundred and sixty-eight children.</s> <s>Pentagon investigators placed the attack on the first day of a two-thousand-target United States-Israel bombing campaign; the United Nations human rights office has called for a war crimes investigation.</s> <s>Defense Secretary <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhɛɡsɛθ">Hegseth</phoneme> offered no apology, saying only that the military is reviewing its findings.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Two of the world's largest Muslim nations are planning a joint visit to Tehran, arguing their shared faith gives them mediation standing that Washington cannot claim.</s> <s>Indonesian President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈprɑboʊwoʊ suˈbiɑntoʊ">Prabowo Subianto</phoneme> has warned he will quit Trump's Board of Peace if Palestine is excluded from any settlement.</s> <s>No date is set, but the visit would mark the highest-level Muslim diplomatic mission to Tehran since the bombing began.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Jimmy Lai, founder of Hong Kong's Apple Daily newspaper, has decided not to appeal his twenty-year sentence under the territory's national security law.</s> <s>Convicted for advocating international sanctions against Beijing, Lai is seventy-eight years old and a British citizen; he would leave prison at ninety-eight.</s> <s>His government in London has made no public commitment to raise his case with Beijing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bahrain deployed teargas on protesters opposing the war — a charged image for a state that hosts the United States Navy's Fifth Fleet while having a Shia Muslim majority.</s> <s>Its 2011 uprising was crushed with Saudi tanks; two men now face charges of assisting an enemy state for marching toward the American embassy.</s> <s>Both facts have rarely been so visible at once.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Venezuela has restored diplomatic ties with the United States after seven years — a reset driven by oil, as the closure of the Strait of Hormuz has made Venezuelan reserves a strategic lifeline.</s> <s>Acting President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdɛlsi roˈdɹiɡɛz">Delcy Rodriguez</phoneme>, governing since Maduro's removal, cited mutual respect as the foundation.</s> <s>What that phrase means for opposition figures and frozen assets has not been spelled out.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>At least two hundred people have died in a collapse at eastern Congo's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ruˈbɑjɑ">Rubaya</phoneme> coltan mine, seventy of them children working unregulated shafts.</s> <s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ruˈbɑjɑ">Rubaya</phoneme> supplies fifteen percent of global coltan — the ore in every smartphone — and the M-23 rebels controlling it have blocked investigators and denied the toll.</s> <s>This is the second collapse this year to kill two hundred people at the same site.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iranian drones struck the airport and a school in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nɑkˈtʃivɑn">Nakhchivan</phoneme>, an Azerbaijani exclave bordering Iran, injuring four people.</s> <s>The attack is the first of this conflict to hit a country with no declared role in the war; Azerbaijan raised its military to full combat readiness and summoned Iran's ambassador.</s> <s>Tehran denied responsibility, and no other actor has been identified.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Bangladesh went two consecutive days without finding a gas seller as the Hormuz closure doubled spot prices, pricing a nation of a hundred and seventy million people out of the open market.</s> <s>Authorities secured two cargo shipments at twice the normal cost and imposed fuel rationing.</s> <s>The longer the strait stays sealed, the fewer options Bangladesh has.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United States has granted India a thirty-day waiver from its own Russia sanctions — a reversal forced by the same war Washington launched.</s> <s>India imports eighty-five percent of its oil, and with Hormuz closed, Russia is its only viable supplier at scale.</s> <s>Renewal in April would require bending the sanctions framework yet further.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A federal judge has ordered the United States to refund a hundred and thirty billion dollars in tariffs the Supreme Court struck down as exceeding presidential emergency authority.</s> <s>With interest, total liability could reach a hundred and seventy-five billion; the White House immediately imposed replacement surcharges.</s> <s>Twenty-four states are already suing to block those as well.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China is preparing to fire the world's first accelerator-driven subcritical reactor — a machine that converts spent nuclear fuel into material that decays in centuries rather than millennia.</s> <s>A successful test would open a path to processing four hundred thousand tonnes of spent fuel stockpiled worldwide, a problem that has stalled nuclear energy's expansion for decades.</s> <s>The United States and Europe studied this approach for years without building it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Half of all Amazonian insect species face lethal heat stress as temperatures rise — with consequences far beyond the rainforest.</s> <s>Unlike Arctic species adapted to extreme swings, tropical insects evolved in stable climates and cannot restructure their proteins fast enough to survive warming.</s> <s>Their collapse would cascade through food systems across Africa, Southeast Asia, and Latin America.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Pentagon has declared Anthropic a supply chain risk — the first time that Cold War national security designation has been used against a domestic technology company.</s> <s>Anthropic refused a military demand to strip safety restrictions from its Claude artificial intelligence models and has threatened to sue; if the ruling stands, federal contractors could be barred from Claude entirely.</s> <s>Such a precedent would test how much of its own safety architecture a private artificial intelligence company must surrender to the state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Proton Mail, marketed as a privacy tool for activists and journalists, helped the F-B-I unmask an anonymous protester by providing account payment records through Swiss legal channels.</s> <s>Encrypted email content cannot be shared, but financial metadata gave investigators enough to identify the user.</s> <s>This is Proton Mail's second known law enforcement disclosure; the first identified a French climate activist.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We return this evening, as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme> reaches <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmɑɡɹɪb">Maghrib</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>